  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and documents:\r\rSigned and Dated Application Form\rCIL Additional Information Form\rSite Location Plan, Drawing No. A0100 Rev 00, prepared by Patalab Architects\rExisting and Proposed Floor Plans, Elevations and Sections, prepared by Patalab Architects\rContaminated Land Risk Assessment, dated June 2026, prepared by STM Environmental\rNoise Impact Assessment, dated July 2026, prepared by RBA Acoustics\rDaylight and Sunlight Assessment, dated June 2026, prepared byEcolytik\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning. \r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied until details of the 4 long-stay cycle parking spaces have been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. \rThese details should demonstrate: \rLocation: Near entrances or main access \rDesign: Stands or wall bars \rSecurity: Secure, overlooked, well-lit \rCoverage: Covered Accessibility: Step-free, no obstructions \rThe cycle parking spaces shall be fully constructed in accordance with the approved details prior to first occupation and shall thereafter be retained for the lifetime of the development. \rReason: To ensure that adequate cycle parking facilities are provided to promote sustainable modes of transport.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied until waste storage and recycling facilities to satisfy the future number of occupiers on site have been provided within the development, in accordance with the Enfield's Household Recycling and Waste Planning Guidance for New Developments (February 2024). Such facilities to be retained for the lifetime of the development.\r\rThe bin store shall be configured to ensure that the doors not open onto the public highway.\r\rReason: To ensure that adequate waste and recycling storage facilities are provided to meet the needs of future occupiers, promote sustainable waste management practices, and support borough-wide recycling targets\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied until details of the means of enclosure for vehicles, pedestrians, and cyclists have been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The enclosures shall be fully constructed in accordance with the approved details prior to first occupation and shall thereafter be retained for the lifetime of the development. \r\rReason: To ensure a safe, secure, and accessible environment for all users of the development, including vehicles, pedestrians, and cyclists, and to maintain the visual quality and functionality of the site\r"
  ],
